**Theorem (`denote_eq_empty_iff`).** The set or language in denote eq empty iff is empty exactly under the stated absence-of-witness condition.

*Proof.* An element of the set in denote eq empty iff would provide exactly the forbidden witness, while any such witness produces an element; hence emptiness is equivalent to its absence. ∎

**Theorem (`nfa_accepts_nonempty_iff`).** The set or language nfa accepts nonempty iff has an element under the hypotheses of the theorem.

*Proof.* Choose witnesses from the nonempty input sets in nfa accepts nonempty iff and combine them using the defining construction. ∎

**Theorem (`nfa_accepts_nonempty_iff_short`).** The language in nfa accepts nonempty iff short is nonempty exactly when it accepts a word shorter than the number of available automaton states.

*Proof.* Repeatedly remove a loop from any longer accepting path for nfa accepts nonempty iff short; finiteness of the state set guarantees a repeated state until a short accepted word remains. ∎

